<h2>Indian organic manure for export</h2>
<p>Organic manure exports from India serve two very different buyers. European and North American horticulture and garden-retail programmes want a natural soil-improvement input, often in retail-format bags. Plantation agriculture in the Gulf, Maldives and Southeast Asia wants bulk organic matter to build soil in low-organic-carbon conditions.</p>

<p>We supply cow manure (powder, granule and cake), vermicompost, poultry manure and general compost — composted, sun-dried, screened and bagged from dairy and agricultural belts across Gujarat, Rajasthan, Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab and Haryana.</p>

<h2>Being precise about "organic"</h2>
<p>This is worth stating plainly because it's where buyers most often get misled in this category. When we say "organic manure", we're describing what the product <em>is</em> — an animal- or plant-origin, non-synthetic soil input. We are not claiming certification under NPOP, USDA Organic, EU Organic or any other standard, and we don't hold such certification.</p>
<p>If your buyer or your market requires certified product, say so at the enquiry stage. We'd rather lose an order at the start than have a shipment rejected at your end over a claim we never should have made.</p>

<h2>Import permits are the practical hurdle</h2>
<p>Animal-origin fertilizers are regulated more tightly than almost anything else we ship. Depending on the destination, you may need a prior import permit, documented composting or heat-treatment declarations, or additional declarations on the phytosanitary certificate. Some markets are simple; others are effectively closed without a permit in hand.</p>
<p>This is the first thing to sort out — before specification, before pricing. {{ site.complianceChecklistCta }}</p>

<h2>What to specify</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Product and form</strong> — cow manure or vermicompost; powder, granule or cake.</li>
  <li><strong>Moisture maximum</strong> — 15–25% typical. Lower moisture means more usable material per shipped tonne.</li>
  <li><strong>Screening mesh</strong> — 2mm, 4mm or your own requirement.</li>
  <li><strong>Packing</strong> — bulk jumbo bags for agriculture, retail bags with artwork for garden-centre programmes.</li>
</ul>

